I've been using the iPad 10 for close to  a month now and I think a lot of you  guys that are considering buying one  need to be very careful for a few  specific reasons in this video I'm going  to give you guys my honest thoughts on  it who should be buying it and at what  price and who should absolutely avoid it  getting right into it I want to start  off with just the tablet itself without  the new keyboard accessory we'll cover  that in just a bit and I want to say  using this as a tablet here at the  office and at home it has actually been  surprisingly good in terms of multimedia  playing games and doing various apps  overall it is a great tablet when you're  looking at it by itself I absolutely  love this blue color even though I'm not  a fan of blue and I think the general  lineup Apple did a great job with the  colors they really pop compared to the  other iPads and that is great for a  consumer device now as you guys know  this is the first time the Apple gave  the base iPad a full redesign so so it's  modern it's clean it looks like the rest  of the more expensive iPad lineup and  that is great when you're buying a  tablet because you're going to keep it  for many years the front of the iPad is  very clean because now we have even  bezels all around without the touch ID  button on the bottom and we have this  touch ID that sits right here at the top  and no matter if you're holding it  vertically you can press with your right  hand or horizontally with your left it  is quite nice and then the volume  buttons also change depending on which  orientation you're holding it now one of  my favorite updates to this iPad are the  speakers previously with the ninth  generation and before we just had a  speaker on the bottom so if you're  holding it landscape you're watching  videos or movies or playing a game all  that sound is coming from their right  hand side now that's hard to show you  guys the difference over video but  here's a quick speaker comparison  compared to the previous generation  [Music]  take me somewhere unfamiliar  [Music]  the speakers are louder they have more  bass it sounds more natural and it  really is a game changer having stereo  speakers instead of just having it from  one side especially for gaming now  talking about gaming I played Call of  Duty at my house and the experience was  great the A14 has no issues keeping up  at 60 FPS the graphics look great the  size is really nice you can hear  footsteps from both sides and actually  track opponents now instead of hearing  it from the right if you want to play  games this is a great tablet to do that  at this price point and as far as  general performance and snappiness this  thing feels nice and fast I don't have  any issues with apps loading up and as  far as web browsing this thing gets 284  runs per minute which is faster than  pretty much most PCS even powerful ones  so web-based applications also are  really nice and quick the only downside  in performance that I noticed is just  some general stuttering because this  does not have promotion so if you have  an iPhone that has that or you have  another tablet you'll notice that it's  just not as smooth but if you don't have  promotion any of your devices it's going  to feel perfectly normal and great the  battery life is also really good you  should be getting at least 10 hours of  use if not more because the A14 that is  in here is actually down clocked  compared to some other devices and that  means that it uses less power so you're  not gonna have any issues with battery  life like you can with an M1 that can  suck a lot more and in terms of charging  it will charge faster than the previous  iPads because it can actually reach 25  watts so that's more than what the  included adapter will give you now it  won't hit 30 Watts like an iPad Air but  that is still an improvement and of  course we finally have a USB type-c port  on the bottom so it's easier to charge  if you have other devices and it's  easier to connect accessories as well  now in our Hands-On test we found out  that it is still stuck to USB 2.0 speeds  even though Apple gave us this new Port  which means that compared to more  expensive iPads it's going to take much  longer to transfer files onto it or off  of it and that is a major bummer but  considering most people that have been  buying this they probably aren't going  to care or they're not going to use that  Port other than to charge now there is  one more issue with this iPad that I did  notice day to day and I think a lot of  people will and that's the fact that the  display is very reflective for some  reason Apple decided to make this iPad  thicker than the iPad Air which means  they had to retool just so that the  display is not laminated now people say  that that makes it so cheaper to replace  the display if it cracks or the actual  screen itself you save the LCD and that  is true you can replace the screen much  cheaper than with the laminated display  now personally I've never cracked a  tablet display if my kids are using it I  use a case and because of that when  you're using it day to day to see way  more Reflections than an iPad Air which  we showed off in our comparison that is  a bummer and you definitely notice that  even in a room like this where it's dim  but if you're outside in a bright room  that makes it much worse and then with  that the contrast is a lot worse when  you're watching videos it is a dramatic  difference as you guys could see so if  you're somebody who thinks you might  crack the display it might be good that  it's not laminated but for the majority  of the time that you're using it you do  notice that downside and I wish Apple  did laminate it now this iPad also has a  secret weapon something that stands out  compared to all the other iPads and  those are the cameras now on the back we  have this camera which is the same on  the iPad Air and comparing it to the  previous iPad 9 which they still sell  the photos look so much better both  regular photos and also if you need to  zoom in now my kids use the cameras on  the back of these so it matters for them  I typically just use it for documents  and that's a nice upgrade now the real  difference is the camera on the front  all the other iPad pads have cameras  that are on the left hand side when  you're holding it in landscape compared  to this one where it is perfectly  centered exactly where it should be and  the mics were upgraded as well so let's  go ahead and take a listen this is the  iPad 10's front facing camera with  front-facing microphones and I'm looking  right at the center of the display and  keep in mind this is Center Stage so you  could also go in a wider View and then  many software will automatically crop if  it's just you or if you have multiple  people in the frame and this is the  previous iPad 9 sitting exactly the same  with a keyboard now I'm looking at the  same exact spot but it looks like I'm  looking way off to the side my head is  cut off as well which is very  interesting and you guys let me know  what you guys think as far as  microphones what difference you hear if  you're somebody who's going to be  FaceTiming you're going to be doing Zoom  or anything else this is the best setup  and the quality is just as good as even  a 12.9 inch iPad Pro but the positioning  is better now the only downside is  Apple's new keyboard now this thing  attaches magnetically to the bottom the  connection is crazy strong that part of  it is awesome and it's a dual design so  the back section which also magnetically  attaches it protects it and you have  this kickstand which I like because you  can adjust the angle and you can also  remove the keyboard if you just want to  prop it up if you're watching something  so overall the design is good there are  only two issues now the first issue is  that the build quality is not as good as  the magic keyboard this whole bottom  section is very flimsy it moves around  it doesn't feel as nice and when you  attach it it doesn't really hold on well  there's no magnets or at least ones that  are strong enough to hold it and in your  bag it actually can rub sideways so if  you get any dust or anything in there  that can scratch up your screen whereas  the magic keyboard is a solid all-in-one  system now I compared it in that review  if you guys want to see it you guys  could check that out out but I have two  other issues with it one issue is the  fact that we don't have any backlighting  and you don't absolutely need to have  that but the other issue is the fact  that it costs 250 dollars and I think at  that price point the build quality  should be better and we should have  backlighting it's one expensive keyboard  especially if you factor in that you can  buy the magic keyboard for 167 dollars  refurbish with a three-month return  policy that just makes this really kind  of overpriced and with that the other  major accessory is also overpriced of  course this uses the original apple  pencil back from 2015 it is very very  old tech for an iPad it's coming out  near 2023 and because Apple got rid of  that port and they're supporting this  one not the magnetically attaching apple  pencil too you can't even pair it you  have to use one of these adapters that  you purchase separately and you have to  use a cable you plug it in it's a very  janky solution and then you can finally  pair it the same thing comes up when you  need to charge it or you can charge it  from an iPhone that has a lightning Port  but still it makes no sense one that  they didn't support the apple pencil two  and two that they didn't include this  adapter in the Box I had to wait about  two weeks to get it even though I  ordered right at pre-open start I think  this adapter if they wanted to go this  method and force you to use the old one  at least it should be in the box when  you factor in shipping packaging all of  that included for people to have the  apple pencil now I was very curious  about the performance and I got to test  it out and yes it is more laggy you see  frame drops there's more delay so  because of that if you are planning to  uh use an apple pencil or to buy one it  just makes this whole thing so expensive  that it doesn't make any logical sense  now if you have it already you can buy  the adapter but buying a new one for 100  bucks with adapter included if it's new  stock I think that doesn't make sense  and the same thing with the keyboard  accessory so because of that my verdict  is if you are just buying the tablet  itself as a tablet and you want  something brand new this one is not bad  now I don't think that 450 is a good  price point 350 would have been amazing  399 would have been still pretty good  considering the limitations but you have  the new design and thankfully we've  already seen it go on sale for 399  dollars now I have links down below  where you guys could check it out or  check out the YouTube shopping feature  right over there you can check it out  there and 3.99 I think that's a price  point that I would recommend this if you  are not going to be buying additional  accessories like the apple pencil or the  keyboard because if you want things like  that you can actually pick up an iPad  Air 4 refurbished for just over 400  bucks and if you add the keyboard which  you can get for 167 you're looking at  572 dollars compared to 700 with this  iPad 10 and the keyboard by itself and  the iPad Air 4 it has better performance  has a laminated display it has better  speakers it is better in almost every  single way I'll have links to that below  as well so that's what I would buy if  you want accessories but if you don't  care about it and you just want the  tablet itself you like the colors I  think at 3.99 it's a buy so that is my  final verdict I wish Apple didn't didn't  make us use this pencil and this  keyboard is a little bit less expensive  but Apple's making everything so  expensive these days so personally what  I would do if you are a power user check  out a refurbished iPad Air 4 has the  same processor in there that would be my  suggestion but going forward when those  are not available it's still a great  tablet for regular normal use but the  pricing is just the biggest issue so you  guys let me know your thoughts would you  pick up one of these or would you  instead go for something maybe a little  bit more expensive or a refurbished  device I want to hear your guys's  opinion click that Circle above if you  guys want to subscribe check out the  comparison to the iPad Air 4 and 5. we  have a dual one right over there this is  the max and I'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

